<section id="cern">
    <img id="subway" src="/images/subway-surfers.gif" draggable="false" />
    <div>
        <h1>World Wide Web</h1>
        The WorldWideWeb (W3) is a wide-area <a>hypermedia</a> information retrieval
        initiative aiming to give universal access to a large universe of documents.
        <p>
            Everything there is online about W3 is linked directly or indirectly
            to this document, including an <a>executive summary</a> of the project,
            <a>Mailing lists</a>, <a>Policy</a>, November's <a>W3 news</a>, <a
                >Frequently Asked Questions</a
            >.
        </p>
        <dl>
            <dt>
                <a>What's out there?</a>
            </dt><dd>
                Pointers to the world's online information, <a>subjects</a>, <a
                    >W3 servers</a
                >, etc.
            </dd><dt>
                <a>Help</a>
            </dt><dd>on the browser you are using</dd><dt>
                <a>Software Products</a>
            </dt><dd>
                A list of W3 project components and their current state. (e.g. <a
                    >Line Mode</a
                >, X11 <a>Viola</a>, <a>NeXTStep</a>, <a>Servers</a>, <a
                    >Tools</a
                >, <a>Mail robot</a>, <a>Library</a>)
            </dd><dt>
                <a>Technical</a>
            </dt><dd>
                Details of protocols, formats, program internals etc
            </dd><dt>
                <a>Bibliography</a>
            </dt><dd>Paper documentation on W3 and references.</dd><dt>
                <a>People</a>
            </dt><dd>A list of some people involved in the project.</dd><dt>
                <a>History</a>
            </dt><dd>A summary of the history of the project.</dd><dt>
                <a>How can I help</a> ?
            </dt><dd>If you would like to support the web..</dd><dt>
                <a>Getting code</a>
            </dt><dd>
                Getting the code by <a>anonymous FTP</a>, etc.
            </dd>
        </dl>
    </div>
</section>
<style>
    #cern {
        position: fixed;
        font-family: Times, serif;
        height: 100vh;
        width: 100vw;
        background-color: white;
        &:not(.active) {
            opacity: 0;
            user-select: none;
            pointer-events: none;
        }
        h1 {
            margin-top: 0;
        }
        a {
            color: blue;
            text-decoration: underline;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;

        div {
            padding: 0.5em;
        }

        #subway {
            width: 0;
            height: 100vh;
            pointer-events: none;
            user-select: none;
            &.active {
                transition: width 0.5s;
                width: 55.1111111111vh;
            }
        }
    }
</style>
<script>
    import { registerClassTransition } from "../lib/slides";

    registerClassTransition("#cern");
    registerClassTransition("#subway");
</script>
